lmn-gpo (1.5.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * SECURITY/DATA-LOSS FIX (regression in 1.3.0/1.4.0): `apply` refused nothing when the
    answers file was missing, mistyped or empty. load_site() returns {} for a non-existent
    path, so every optional package read as disabled and _retire() unlinked and DELETED its
    GPO -- up to 29 GPOs on a three-school site, without backup and with exit code 0.
    `apply` now aborts with exit 2 unless the answers file exists and is non-empty; the
    deliberate "no optional features" run needs the new --defaults flag.
  * _retire: take a `samba-tool gpo backup` into /var/backups/lmn-gpo/<timestamp>-<name>
    before deleting, and never retire on a precondition that depends on a FILE rather than
    an operator answer. `requires: wallpaper` is now reported and skipped instead of
    deleting the branding GPO -- the source checkout and the .deb use different wallpaper
    directories, so the documented upgrade path silently destroyed it.
  * Exclusions no longer fail open silently: when filter_deny or filter_deny_read resolves
    to no group (missing d_nopxe, typo in teachernb), apply prints a loud warning naming the
    pack and token and exits non-zero. Previously nothing was written and nothing was said,
    so the GPO reached exactly the devices it was meant to spare.
  * Global packs are linked domain-wide at OU=SCHOOLS, so their exclusion groups are now
    resolved against ALL detected schools, not only the ones selected for the run. Before,
    `apply --school a` left school b's teacher notebooks unexcluded while still applying.
  * Wi-Fi: both packages now follow `teachernb` instead of hard-wiring @nopxe, so a custom
    teacher-notebook group is honoured for Wi-Fi as it already was for power/lock/proxy.
    13-wlan-psk additionally carries filter_deny_read: ['@role-student'].
    NOTE: that denies students read on the GPO object only. sysvolreset writes a fixed ACL
    template, so the startup script FILE containing the passphrase stays readable by
    Authenticated Users. Documented in the pack and the README; the PSK must be treated as
    obtainable by students. Pre-staging the profile in the LINBO image avoids this.
  * setup: write site.yaml as 0600 in a 0700 directory (it holds plaintext Wi-Fi PSKs and
    the Veyon bind password); previously 0644.
  * apply: escape RFC 4515 specials in the custom teachernb group lookup, so a CN containing
    '*' or parentheses cannot silently match the wrong group or nothing at all.
  * Power: the display no longer switches off on its own. The timeout is now the site.yaml
    key display_off_seconds and defaults to 0 = never, so a machine driving a beamer or an
    interactive panel does not go dark mid-lesson. Set it to a number of seconds to restore
    a timeout. The screen still LOCKS after 30 min (pack 04-sperren) — the display then
    shows the lock screen instead of going dark; those are two separate settings.
  * gpp: use a generic NetBIOS name in a docstring example instead of a real customer one.
  * lmn-gpo-check.ps1: distinguish all-user from per-user Wi-Fi profiles. Only an all-user
    profile connects before login; a per-user one (a manual connect from the Wi-Fi flyout)
    is now reported as a failure instead of OK.

 -- Kevin Stenzel <kevin@ks98.de>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

lmn-gpo (1.4.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Proxy: exclude teacher notebooks (teachernb, by default the d_nopxe device group) from
    all five 12-proxy-* packages. They roam out of the school network, where the school proxy
    is unreachable; because the proxy is written to the real WinINET key rather than a
    Policies branch it tattoos, so an excluded notebook would otherwise stay pointed at an
    unreachable proxy and lose internet access off-site.
  * New catalog field filter_deny_read plus GpoEngine.deny_read. For the user-scope role
    proxy packages a plain deny-apply would be a silent no-op: those settings only reach a
    user through loopback processing, where Apply Group Policy is evaluated against the USER
    while (since MS16-072) the GPO list is retrieved in the COMPUTER's context. A device
    group can therefore only be excluded by denying it Read, so the machine never retrieves
    the GPO. The computer-scope packages (12-proxy-base, 12-proxy-zone-schule) use the
    ordinary filter_deny.
  * Note: removing the policy does not clear an already-provisioned client, because the
    WinINET proxy values tattoo. Reset affected profiles once, e.g. by deleting ProxyEnable
    under HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Internet Settings.

